  "designBoundaries": [
    "The new recovery begins from the actual landed orientation and angular velocity. A forward twist completes only the remaining revolution; orthogonal swing unwinds with preserved initial angular velocity. Nearly upright landings can step out.",
    "The waist offset and limb secondary motion release on finite smooth curves. The existing recovery duration, gameplay drive, mash speedup, linear motion, collision and replay random stream retain their ownership.",
    "Support-loss re-entry retains its current pose; missing/steep floor and fatal breakup behavior keep their existing paths. Exact support checks remain test-only.",
    "All new state is fixed per player. Sampling creates no scene bodies, vectors or arrays, and makes no world queries. Coefficients are cached at handoff; finished swing and completed recovery bypass unnecessary math.",
    "Rendered orientation audits normalize decomposed quaternions because inherited nonuniform character proportions can otherwise inflate angleTo readings."
  ],
